# build-profile.json5 is deliberately NOT ignored, unlike the RNOH scaffold's
# default. It holds real project settings — compatibleSdkVersion,
# targetSdkVersion — that a fresh clone needs; compatibleSdkVersion in
# particular was hand-bumped to satisfy react-native-document-picker's
# harmony port (see harmony/README.md). Ignoring it, as the scaffold does by
# default, would silently drop that fix on every fresh checkout.
#
# Caution if you ever sign the HAP locally through DevEco (File > Project
# Structure > Signing Configs > Automatically generate signature): that
# writes your own certificate paths into this file's `signingConfigs` array.
# Don't commit those — revert that section, or ask before committing if
# you're unsure what changed.

/local.properties
/.idea
**/build
/.hvigor
.cxx
/.clangd
/.clang-format
/.clang-tidy
/oh_modules
hvigorw
hvigorw.bat
hvigor/hvigor-wrapper.js
